<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0
             http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>com.aether</groupId>
    <artifactId>aether-playwright-java</artifactId>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>

    <name>AETHER Playwright Java Validation Framework</name>
    <description>
        AETHER-generated Playwright-Java + TestNG automation framework.
        Source: Banking_Login_TC_1.pdf (TC_001 – TC_008)
        Requirement: REQ-BANK-AUTH-001
        Target AUT: http://localhost:3000 (mock_aut/server.js)
    </description>

    <!--
        T2.3 — the compiler level was 11 and this project has **never compiled**.

        `src/main/java/com/aether/framework/core/PlaywrightManager.java:42` uses a switch
        expression, which needs `-source 14` or higher; javac refused it with "switch
        expressions are not supported in -source 11". Nothing had noticed, because until
        Phase 2 nothing in AETHER ever ran `mvn` against this tree: svc-tew's image carried
        no toolchain, so TEEA returned SKIPPED without attempting a build.

        Found by the first real execution — svc-runner reported COMPLETED with exit code 1
        and no Surefire reports, which svc-tew correctly reported as NO_TESTS_DISCOVERED.
        Correct, and a diagnosis of the wrong thing: the suite had not been *run*.

        17 rather than 14, matching the JDK in svc-runner's image
        (`maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-17`). This project is TD14's verification target, so a
        source level its own runner cannot compile makes T2.3's acceptance criterion
        unreachable. Nothing else in the repository reads these values. Recorded as
        ADR §6.29.
    -->
    <properties>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <maven.compiler.source>17</maven.compiler.source>
        <maven.compiler.target>17</maven.compiler.target>
        <playwright.version>1.44.0</playwright.version>
        <testng.version>7.8.0</testng.version>
        <extentreports.version>5.1.1</extentreports.version>
        <slf4j.version>2.0.9</slf4j.version>
        <surefire.version>3.2.2</surefire.version>
        <jackson.version>2.16.1</jackson.version>
    </properties>

    <dependencies>
        <!-- Microsoft Playwright for Java -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.microsoft.playwright</groupId>
            <artifactId>playwright</artifactId>
            <version>${playwright.version}</version>
        </dependency>

        <!-- TestNG -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.testng</groupId>
            <artifactId>testng</artifactId>
            <version>${testng.version}</version>
        </dependency>

        <!-- ExtentReports — rich HTML test report -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.aventstack</groupId>
            <artifactId>extentreports</artifactId>
            <version>${extentreports.version}</version>
        </dependency>

        <!-- SLF4J simple binding -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.slf4j</groupId>
            <artifactId>slf4j-simple</artifactId>
            <version>${slf4j.version}</version>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Jackson — JSON fixture parsing -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.fasterxml.jackson.core</groupId>
            <artifactId>jackson-databind</artifactId>
            <version>${jackson.version}</version>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.11.0</version>
                <configuration>
                    <!-- Explicit plugin config overrides the maven.compiler.* properties
                         above, so both had to change. Leaving this at 11 would have kept
                         the build failing while the properties said otherwise, which is
                         the harder version of the same defect to find. -->
                    <source>17</source>
                    <target>17</target>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>

            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>${surefire.version}</version>
                <configuration>
                    <suiteXmlFiles>
                        <suiteXmlFile>testng.xml</suiteXmlFile>
                    </suiteXmlFiles>
                    <!-- Never fail build — capture all results -->
                    <testFailureIgnore>true</testFailureIgnore>
                    <!--
                      There was a `<systemPropertyVariables><BASE_URL>` here and it was
                      read by nothing. ConfigReader looks up the *key* `base.url` as a
                      system property and only then the environment variable `BASE_URL`
                      (dots to underscores, upper-cased); a system property literally
                      named BASE_URL matches neither step. So the value that took effect
                      was always config.properties', and `mvn test -DBASE_URL=…` — which
                      this project's README documented — silently did nothing.

                      Removed rather than corrected to `<base.url>`, because a system
                      property is priority 1 and would then shadow the environment
                      variable svc-runner sets to point the suite at the compose AUT
                      (ADR §6.27). The two working overrides, highest first:

                        mvn test -Dbase.url=http://localhost:4000
                        BASE_URL=http://mock-aut:3000 mvn test

                      Nothing is declared in its place on purpose: surefire hands the
                      forked JVM this process's environment, which is how BASE_URL
                      arrives from the container. Pinning it here would undo that.

                      ADR §6.27.
                    -->
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
